      "Language": "dan",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The use of balloon angioplasty (PTCA) for stenosis of the left main coronary artery has been associated with poor long-term results, but, according to a recent report, PTCA with stent implantation appears to be attended by acceptable complication rates, as compared with coronary artery bypass grafting. This paper reports a case of successful cardiopulmonary resuscitation of long duration, followed by successful balloon angioplasty and stent implantation in acute thrombosis of a stenosis of the left main coronary artery."},
